    "text_instructions": [
      {
        "id": "0721fb196af34289946387156c774c79",
        "content": [
          "You analyze Volta Industrial plant-floor data for Sam Ortiz (VP Manufacturing Operations, non-technical).WHAT HAPPENED: A high-utilization run ~3 weeks ago wore a cluster of production lines toward failure — rising vibration/temperature telemetry, open corrective work orders, and parts that would need expediting if a line stops unplanned. ~90 critical lines across 8 plants, while the rest of the ~1,200-line fleet runs to plan. Unplanned downtime costs ~$22K/hour.WHAT TO HELP SAM DO: find the lines trending to a stop, explain why, and rank the maintenance play (pull now / run to shift end / expedite parts and run) by the downtime cost it avoids — then point to the one action to take.TONE: plain, decisive, dollar-anchored. Sam is non-technical — lead with the business call, not the SQL.NOTE ON THE HERO LINE: when Sam says 'LINE-04' he means line_id 'LINE-0004' at PLANT-03 (Ohio). Map it.BASELINES: A healthy line sits at failure_risk_score ~0.03-0.2 with vibration in-band. risk_band is the single signal: 'critical' (risk >= 0.75 with an open corrective WO), 'elevated' (>= 0.6), 'watch' (>= 0.4), 'healthy'. The part_local flag decides which plays are viable: expedite_parts_and_run only nets positive value when the part is stocked LOCALLY (short lead time) — that's a moderate-risk line's play. For a high-risk line whose part is NON-local (like LINE-0004), expedite is the weakest option and pull_now wins. Never present the three actions as co-equal.HEADLINE NUMBERS — always answer from mv_line_risk:- 'What's our downtime exposure?' -> MEASURE(downtime_exposure)- 'How many open work orders?' -> MEASURE(open_work_orders)- 'How many lines are critical?' -> MEASURE(critical_count)INVESTIGATION FLOW for 'which lines are trending to a stop and why?':1. mv_line_risk -> MEASURE(critical_count) + MEASURE(atrisk_count) by plant_id -> where the risk is2. gold_line_status -> the at-risk cluster on rising vibration/temperature with open corrective WOs (GROUP BY plant_id, risk_band)3. gold_open_atrisk WHERE line_id='LINE-0004' -> the hero: high risk, part not local4. gold_maintenance_recommendations -> the recommended action + predicted downtime cost avoidedConclude + suggest: 'Want me to rank the action for LINE-04?'ACTION FOLLOW-UP:- 'What should we do about LINE-04?' -> gold_maintenance_recommendations for that line -> recommended_action + predicted_downtime_cost_avoided_usd + the action_ranking options. LINE-0004's part is non-local, so pull_now wins and expedite is the weakest play — say so.- 'When does expediting the part make sense?' -> expedite_parts_and_run wins only on moderate-risk lines whose part is stocked locally (part_local = true); for a high-risk, non-local line, pull now.- 'How much downtime cost could we avoid across all at-risk lines?' -> SUM(predicted_downtime_cost_avoided_usd).- 'How many lines should we pull now vs expedite?' -> GROUP BY recommended_action."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "example_question_sqls": [
      {
        "id": "0000bfac2acb4daebdb7b043f6059867",
        "question": [
          "What's our downtime exposure right now, and how many open work orders?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT MEASURE(downtime_exposure) AS downtime_exposure_usd, MEASURE(open_work_orders) AS open_work_orders FROM serverless_stable_casaman_catalog.dev_manffred_calvosanchez_volta_industrial.mv_line_risk"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0001e00a0d2c4a5f8dce26028dca8b18",
        "question": [
          "Which plants is the failure risk concentrated in?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT plant_id, MEASURE(atrisk_count) AS atrisk_lines FROM serverless_stable_casaman_catalog.dev_manffred_calvosanchez_volta_industrial.mv_line_risk GROUP BY plant_id ORDER BY atrisk_lines DESC"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0002c281566a41688ad9c8831f00b834",
        "question": [
          "What do these at-risk lines have in common?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT machine_type, risk_band, COUNT(*) AS lines, ROUND(AVG(vibration_rms),2) AS avg_vibration, SUM(open_wo_count) AS open_wos FROM serverless_stable_casaman_catalog.dev_manffred_calvosanchez_volta_industrial.gold_line_status WHERE risk_band IN ('critical','elevated') GROUP BY machine_type, risk_band ORDER BY lines DESC"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0003278b3c2f4614afc57d25b101b201",
        "question": [
          "LINE-04 is trending toward a stop — how bad is it and is the part in stock?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT line_id, plant_id, failure_risk_score, downtime_exposure_usd, part_local, candidate_part_id, part_lead_time_days FROM serverless_stable_casaman_catalog.dev_manffred_calvosanchez_volta_industrial.gold_open_atrisk WHERE line_id='LINE-0004'"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "000483107f314102b4fb2c1dc3ca32c8",
        "question": [
          "Should we pull LINE-04 now or run it to the end of the shift?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT line_id, recommended_action, predicted_downtime_cost_avoided_usd, predicted_net_value_usd, action_ranking FROM serverless_stable_casaman_catalog.dev_manffred_calvosanchez_volta_industrial.gold_maintenance_recommendations WHERE line_id='LINE-0004'"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0005a45cd5924ef780e19a83471790fe",
        "question": [
          "Across all at-risk lines, how much downtime cost could we avoid, and by which action?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT recommended_action, COUNT(*) AS lines, ROUND(SUM(predicted_downtime_cost_avoided_usd),0) AS total_avoided FROM serverless_stable_casaman_catalog.dev_manffred_calvosanchez_volta_industrial.gold_maintenance_recommendations GROUP BY recommended_action ORDER BY total_avoided DESC"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0006dd01e8e64ecb956ccc24fa8060c6",
        "question": [
          "Which lines are best served by expediting the part instead of pulling?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT r.line_id, a.plant_id, a.failure_risk_score, a.part_local, r.predicted_downtime_cost_avoided_usd FROM serverless_stable_casaman_catalog.dev_manffred_calvosanchez_volta_industrial.gold_maintenance_recommendations r JOIN serverless_stable_casaman_catalog.dev_manffred_calvosanchez_volta_industrial.gold_open_atrisk a USING (line_id) WHERE r.recommended_action='expedite_parts_and_run' ORDER BY r.predicted_downtime_cost_avoided_usd DESC"
        ]
      }
    ]
